export anchor SubwayMapStyle:
    number: 125
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Subway map
    idea: Each project is a coloured transit line running from its start to a terminus at the due date, with station dots, a train marker at the current percent, and the navigation drawn as a line you ride.
    base: light
    palette:
        platform: #f4f4ef, the page
        white: #ffffff, panels, fields and station dots
        ink: #111111, text, 2px borders, the primary button and the train marker
        greyLine: #56565a, the nav line, meta text and last week in the chart
        signYellow: #ffd23f, the service notice, time tags and avatar, never text
        lineW: #b3261e, Website redesign and the Behind octagon
        lineM: #1d4ed8, Mobile app 2.0, this week in the chart and focus
        lineQ: #15803d, Q4 customer survey
        lineB: #7e22ce, Billing migration
        lineS: #8a5a00, Spring catalogue
        lineO: #0f766e, Onboarding emails
        onTrack: #15703a, the filled circle with a tick
        atRisk: #9a4d00, the triangle with a bar
    type:
        One stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Segoe UI, sans-serif.
        The greeting is 40px 800 at 1.1 with tight tracking, summary numbers
        44px 800, section titles 22px 800, line names 18px 800, body 16px at
        1.45, meta 14px 600 grey, time tags 14px bold monospace.
    layout:
        A white top bar with a dark rounded square logo showing a yellow line
        and two stations, then a pill search, a black pill New project
        button, a round bell and a yellow avatar. Under it the nav is a thick
        grey line with a white station dot per item, the current Home a large
        interchange ring with the words you are here. The greeting is a white
        platform sign with a 16px black left edge, and a yellow service notice
        on the right says 4 tasks are overdue. Four boards with a grey top
        band hold the numbers, the overdue one with a red band. The Project
        network panel lists six lines. Each row has a coloured round code
        letter, the name over a linked rings team tag, then a 10px track in
        the line colour, solid up to the percent and dashed beyond, white
        station rings at 0, 25, 50 and 75 percent, a terminus bar at the
        end, a black pill train marker showing the percent, and below it the
        task count and Terminus with the due date. Status sits on the right.
        Below, a chart panel draws the 14 days as a thick metro line with
        ring stations and values, grey for last week and blue for this week,
        joined by an interchange ring at Saturday 24, with pill labels for
        the week totals. Recent arrivals lists activity with a coloured line
        roundel and a yellow time tag. Below 980px status drops under the
        name and the track goes full width, below 640px the nav line scrolls
        sideways inside itself and boards go two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between rows and boards, 24px panel gaps and 32px between sections.
    density: Medium. One full width line per project, read left to right.
    corners: Full rounds for stations, roundels, pills and buttons, 8px on panels, a square platform sign.
    borders: 2px ink on every panel and control and a 16px ink edge on the greeting sign.
    shadows: None. Contrast comes from thick lines and white station dots.
    icons:
        Solid transit pictograms at 20px with a white inner mark, a circle
        with a tick for On track, a triangle with a bar for At risk and an
        octagon with a bar for Behind. Linked rings mark team interchanges.
    focus: A 3px blue outline offset 2px with a 6px white gap ring around it.
    tone: Station announcements, such as Service notice, you are here, Terminus 14 Nov and Recent arrivals.
